    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently, when opening a directory with neovim (e.g. `nvim ~/.config/nvim`) it'll throw you into netrw.\r\n\r\nInstead I suggest a behavior similar to [`stevearc/oil.nvim`](https://github.com/stevearc/oil.nvim), where it opens its file explorer instead when `use_as_default_explorer` is enabled.\r\n\r\nTo me, this would seem a lot more ergonomic.",
