        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Oh, thanks for the heads up. Works like a charm! I do feel silly for not figuring that out myself, especially because I even had `event = { \"VimEnter\" }` set for 'oil.nvim' but removed it for some reason when switching to 'mini.files'.\r\n\r\nStill, I think it might be worth mentioning this in the README, unless I missed it.\r\n\r\nIn case someone else runs into the same issue: Setting `{ event = \"VimEnter\" }` when using 'lazy.nvim' doesn't not seem to suffice, as `mini.files` will still load in too late and not open right away, but also open twice when calling `MiniFiles.open()` for the first time after opening Vim. `lazy = false` does need to be set to have it work properly.",
            "created_at": "2024-10-07T22:48:33Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1264#issuecomment-2398059173",
